; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Playing Turtle: the Circle
; CATEGORY: Classic Logo
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     Mindstorms, circles, REPEAT, polygons
; SUMMARY:  Papert's turtle circle: a little forward, a little turn, 360 times, and then polygons that slowly turn into circles.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Across the top, four circles are drawn slowly, each with a bigger
;   step. Along the bottom, polygons with 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 12 and 36 sides
;   show how a shape with many sides starts to look round.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch the turtle walk. Then try walking a circle
;   yourself on the floor: a tiny step, a tiny turn, over and over.
;   Type  clean circle 3  in the command center for a bigger circle.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * REPEAT and the "total trip" of 360 degrees
;   * a bigger step makes a bigger circle, the turning stays the same
;   * a circle is a polygon with very many very short sides
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make a half circle with REPEAT 180.
;   * Turn LEFT instead of RIGHT. Where does the circle go?
;   * Find the step that makes a circle exactly 200 wide.
; ============================================================

; In Mindstorms (1980) Seymour Papert describes children finding out how
; to draw a circle by "playing turtle": walking in a circle themselves
; and noticing that they take a small step forward, turn a little, and
; do it again. Written down, that is  REPEAT 360 [FORWARD 1 RIGHT 1].
; Papert called this kind of learning "body syntonic": the child's own
; body helps them understand the turtle.

; CIRCLE draws slowly, so you can see the turtle walk. Every 10 steps it
; waits a moment.
to circle :step
  repeat 360 [
    forward :step
    right 1
    if (remainder repcount 10) = 0 [wait 1]
  ]
end

; A circle made with step S has a perimeter of 360 * S, so its width is
; 360 * S / pi, about 115 * S. We use that to place them in a row.
to circle.at :x :step :color
  penup
  setxy :x - 115 * :step / 2 120
  setheading 0
  pendown
  setpencolor :color
  circle :step
  penup
  setxy :x - 25 120 - 57.5 * :step - 28
  label (sentence "step :step)
end

; A polygon with the same perimeter (240 steps), so they all
; have about the same size and are easy to compare.
to polygon :sides
  repeat :sides [forward 240 / :sides right 360 / :sides]
end

to polygon.row
  localmake "x -370
  foreach [3 4 5 6 8 12 36] [
    penup setxy :x -170 setheading 0 pendown
    setpencolor [40 90 200]
    polygon ?
    penup setxy :x + 30 -270
    label ?
    make "x :x + 108
    wait 15
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [252 250 240]
setpensize 3
setlabelheight 16
circle.at -300 0.5 [230 80 60]
circle.at -175 1 [240 160 30]
circle.at 0 1.5 [60 160 80]
circle.at 250 2 [120 80 200]
polygon.row
